<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "zfs.dataset.converter">
<!ENTITY author    "MajorPain007">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.08.08.04">
<!ENTITY md5       "1129be50fc3800e7fa3f06c4625dde55">
<!ENTITY launch    "Settings/ZFSDatasetConverter">
<!ENTITY github    "MajorPain007/zfs-dataset-converter">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main/src/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY pkgURL    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main/archive">
<!ENTITY pluginDir "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY configDir "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY tmpDir    "/tmp/&name;">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" launch="&launch;"
        pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        min="6.12.0"
        icon="database">

<CHANGES>
## Version 2026.08.08.04 — Folder picker and snapshot filtering

- Restore destination is now a path picker: click the field and Unraid's own
  file tree opens, the same widget the Docker templates use. Typing a path by
  hand still works. If the widget is unavailable a built-in folder browser
  takes over, so the feature never simply disappears.
- Snapshot Manager: filter field. Plain substring, or `*` and `?` as wildcards,
  case insensitive - e.g. `hourly` or `auto-daily-2026-07*`. The summary shows
  "N of M shown" with the size of the filtered set.
- Select-all now covers exactly the rows the filter leaves visible, so a
  pattern plus one click selects everything matching it.
- Hold and Release work on a whole selection, not just one row at a time.
  Already-held and not-held snapshots count as success instead of erroring.

## Version 2026.08.08.03 — Fix file selection and snapshot comparison

- Fix "ReferenceError: updateSelCount is not defined" when browsing a
  snapshot. The rewrite that moved restores into a background worker deleted
  snapSelectAll() and updateSelCount() along with the old restore code - they
  sat between the two functions being replaced. Selecting files and the
  select-all checkbox in the snapshot browser work again.
- Fix "Unable to obtain diffs: Not an earlier snapshot from the same fs".
  zfs diff needs the older snapshot first; picking them the other way round
  failed. The two snapshots are now ordered by creation time automatically, so
  the selection order no longer matters, and the summary states the direction
  actually compared (older -> newer).
- Clearer error when two snapshots genuinely cannot be compared, e.g. after a
  rollback.
- New check `tests/js_checks.py`, wired into the suite: every function called
  from the page, every function referenced from an on* attribute and every
  getElementById target must exist. `php -l` and `node --check` both accept a
  call to a missing function - that is exactly how the bug above shipped.

## Version 2026.08.08.02 — Hotfix: GUI rendered as plain text

- Fix the settings page showing raw JavaScript instead of the interface, with
  no dataset lists and no working buttons.
  Unraid runs `.page` bodies through a Markdown pass unless the header sets
  `Markdown="false"`. That pass eats `*` characters (a cron string like
  `*/5 * * * *` loses them) and turns indented blocks into code blocks, which
  stops the browser from ever entering script mode - so the whole script block
  is parsed as markup and shown as text. Removing the comment lines in
  2026.08.08.01 changed the blank-line and indentation structure enough to
  trigger it.
- Two fixes, belt and braces:
  1. The page header now sets `Markdown="false"`, the same way Unraid's own
     Plugins.page does.
  2. The markup moved to `ZFSDatasetConverterPage.php`, which the `.page`
     includes. Unraid now only ever sees a four-line page body, so nothing it
     does to page content can reach the markup.
- `tests/run.sh` guards both: the header directive and the page staying minimal.

## Version 2026.08.08.01 — Reliability + feature release

### New: Snapshot Manager
- Full snapshot table with used / referenced / creation per snapshot, sorted
  biggest first, plus how much space snapshots cost per dataset
  (`usedbysnapshots`). Answers "which snapshot is eating my pool".
- Multi-select delete, per-snapshot hold / release, and dataset rollback.
- Rollback is double-gated: a warning listing the newer snapshots that will be
  destroyed, then the exact snapshot name has to be typed back. The backend
  refuses the request unless the confirmation matches.

### New: zfs diff
- Compare any two snapshots of a dataset, or a snapshot against the live
  filesystem, directly in the snapshot browser. Added / removed / modified /
  renamed entries are colour coded with counts.

### New: Replication (zfs send / recv)
- Per-job replication to a second pool or another machine over SSH.
- Incremental by default: each job keeps its own `@zdc-send-JOBID-TIMESTAMP`
  checkpoint snapshots, so replication never breaks when the regular auto
  snapshots are pruned. The newest snapshot present on both sides is used as
  the incremental base.
- Dry run, per-job connectivity test, background worker with a live log.
- SSH is key-based only; the plugin never handles passwords.
- `zfs recv -F` (destination rollback) is opt-in per job, off by default.
- Job config is parsed by PHP, not by another hand-rolled shell JSON parser.

### New: age-based retention and free-space pruning
- Optional maximum age per snapshot type, on top of the existing count-based
  retention. A snapshot goes when it is beyond the newest N *or* older than
  the configured number of days.
- Free-space target (e.g. 100G or 10%): if the pool drops below it, the oldest
  auto snapshots are pruned until it is met again. Held snapshots and the
  newest snapshot of each dataset/type are never touched.
- Snapshots with a `zfs hold` are excluded from every pruning pass.

### New: restore in the background
- Restores run in a detached worker with a progress indicator. A large folder
  used to hit PHP's execution limit and leave a half-restored tree behind.

### New: dry run and diagnostics
- "Dry Run" reports exactly what would be created and pruned, changing nothing.
- "Diagnostics" downloads a support bundle: config, logs, cron state, pool and
  snapshot inventory. Private keys are excluded.

### Scheduling (this is why snapshots were sometimes missing)
- Cron jobs are now installed the Unraid way: `/etc/cron.d/zfs.dataset.converter`
  and `/etc/cron.d/zfs.dataset.converter-snapshots` plus `update_cron`.
  Entries written directly with `crontab -` were silently dropped whenever
  anything else on the system rebuilt the crontab (other plugins, User
  Scripts, schedule changes). A verification step falls back to the old
  method if a given Unraid build does not pick the file up.
- Cron expressions are validated (5 fields, safe characters) before being
  written. A malformed custom expression can no longer break the whole root
  crontab and take Unraid's own jobs (mover, parity check) down with it.
- Cron is re-registered on every array start via a `disks_mounted` event hook,
  not only at plugin install time.
- Legacy duplicate crontab entries from older versions are removed on upgrade.

### Snapshot manager
- Scheduling is now due-based instead of clock-based. A type is taken when the
  current period has no snapshot yet, so a missed cron tick, a delayed run,
  a server that was powered off at 02:00 or an unusual cron interval can no
  longer skip a snapshot. Previously anything but an exact `minute == 00` hit
  meant that hour/day was lost for good.
- Single-instance locking (flock) — overlapping runs could race while pruning.
- Pruning now runs every cycle, so lowering a retention value takes effect
  immediately instead of waiting for the next snapshot of that type.
- Prune matching is anchored on the part after `@` (hardening: substring
  matching could in principle select a foreign snapshot for deletion).
- Fixed the JSON parser. The old `s/\\\///g` did not unescape `\/` — it
  deleted it, AND the substitution reset Perl's `$1`, so the key name was
  lost and the whole dataset silently disappeared from the list. Any config
  written with slash-escaping was therefore skipped entirely, which is the
  real cause of "no snapshots are ever created". Now handles `\/`, `\"`,
  `\\` and `\uXXXX` correctly.
- Guards against running before the array is up (no more spurious
  "dataset does not exist" errors after a reboot).
- Pool capacity warning + Unraid notification when free space runs low.
- Unraid notification when a run finishes with errors.
- Machine-readable run result in `/tmp/.../snapshot_status.json`.
- "Run Now" no longer burns the current daily/weekly/monthly/yearly period;
  it creates whatever is actually due and says so when nothing is.

### Converter
- Stopped containers and VMs are now restarted from an EXIT trap. Pressing
  "Stop", an OOM kill or an rsync failure used to leave everything powered off.
- rsync now uses `-aHAX --numeric-ids`: hardlinks, ACLs and extended
  attributes are preserved. Plain `-a` silently dropped all three.
- Aborts if a freshly created dataset is not mounted at the expected path —
  rsync would otherwise write into the parent dataset and the data would be
  shadowed as soon as the child mounted.
- Dataset names with spaces are rejected up front with a pointer to the
  "replace spaces" option, instead of failing after the folder was renamed.
- `dataset_exists` uses a literal match; dots in dataset names were treated
  as regex wildcards and could produce false positives.
- Refuses to start when a `*_temp` directory already exists.
- Validation counts all entries (symlinks, empty dirs), not just regular files.

### Housekeeping / PHP
- `/tmp` is a RAM disk: `snapshots.log` is trimmed and old run logs are pruned.
  Previously the snapshot log grew without limit for as long as the server ran.
- `get_snapshot_status.php` tails the log from the end instead of loading the
  whole file into memory, and reports cron health, pool capacity and the
  structured result of the last run.
- `get_logs.php`: removed `str_starts_with` (PHP 8 only, fatal on PHP 7) and
  recovers when a log file is rotated underneath the viewer.
- Restore no longer times out mid-copy on large folders, refuses to write into
  a read-only `.zfs` path and preserves ACLs/xattrs/hardlinks.
- `run_auto.sh` validates every value before templating and aborts if any
  placeholder is left unsubstituted.
- New setting: minimum pool free space (%) before warning.
- Build script syntax-checks every file and keeps version/md5 in the manifest
  in sync automatically.
- Test suite (`tests/run.sh`) and GitHub Actions CI: syntax, PHP 7
  compatibility, Unraid pitfalls, and behavioural regression tests for the
  cron validator and the JSON parser.
- Releases are published as GitHub Release assets from a tag.

## Version 2026.04.12.10
- Auto-save: all settings are saved automatically 800 ms after the last
  change — no Save buttons needed. Small "✓ Saved" indicator appears in
  the header and fades after 2 s. Covers: all left-column inputs, all
  snapshot settings, dataset add/remove/toggle, retention overrides.
- Remove "Save Settings" and "Save Snapshot Settings" buttons

## Version 2026.04.12.09
- Fix settings loss: "Save Settings" (left column) was wiping all
  snapshot settings (snapshots_enabled, snap_hourly, cron schedule etc.)
  because save_settings.php wrote empty strings for POST keys that were
  absent. Now merges with existing settings.cfg — only keys present in
  the POST request are updated.
- Fix PHP type hints in save_settings.php error handler (PHP 7 compat)

## Version 2026.04.12.08
- Add checkboxes to snapshot browser for multi-select restore
- "Restore Selected (N)" button with sequential restore + progress counter
- Fix directory restore: folder is now recreated by name inside the
  destination (e.g. restoring "traefik/" to /mnt/user/Backup →
  /mnt/user/Backup/traefik/ with contents inside)
- Restore to original location vs. custom destination now handled
  separately in PHP for correct path construction in both cases

## Version 2026.04.12.07
- Fix restore: destination is now always treated as a folder — files are
  restored inside it with their original filename (e.g. restoring
  traefik.yml to /mnt/user/Backup → /mnt/user/Backup/traefik.yml).
  Previously cp renamed the file to the destination name when the folder
  did not yet exist.

## Version 2026.04.12.06
- Fix restore to absolute destination path (e.g. /mnt/user/Backup):
  zdc_safe_path() was stripping the leading slash and appending the path
  to the dataset mountpoint, resulting in wrong restore location.
  Absolute paths are now handled by a separate zdc_safe_abs_path() helper.

## Version 2026.04.12.05
- Fix snapshots never creating: PHP json_encode() escaped slashes as \/
  causing snapshot_manager.sh to look for "cache\/appdata" instead of
  "cache/appdata" — fixed with JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES in PHP + unescape
  in Perl parser as fallback for existing configs

## Version 2026.04.12.04
- Pure two-column layout: Folder Scanner / Conversion / Live Log moved
  into left column — no more full-width block at the bottom
- snapshot_manager.sh: when dataset not found, log all available ZFS
  datasets so the correct name can be identified
- snapshot_manager.sh: silent zfs failures now logged as
  "no error output from zfs" instead of an empty suffix

## Version 2026.04.12.02
- Full-width two-column layout: settings left, snapshots+browser right
- Folder Scanner / Conversion / Live Log span full width at bottom
- Snapshot dataset table gets horizontal scroll on narrow screens
- snapshot_manager.sh now captures and logs actual zfs error messages
  (was: silently swallowed via 2>/dev/null)
- Add dataset-existence check before attempting snapshot creation

## Version 2026.04.12.01
- Add snapshot log viewer (shows last 30 lines of snapshots.log)
- Show configured dataset count in snapshot status bar
- Warn when "Run Now" is clicked but no datasets are configured
- Log section opens automatically on Run Now; View Log button to toggle manually
- get_snapshot_status.php now returns dataset_count + recent_log

## Version 2026.04.11.03
- Fix snapshot browser empty response: add missing CSRF token to POST request

## Version 2026.04.11.02
- Fix snapshot browser empty response (remove ob_start, use direct echo)

## Version 2026.04.11.01
- Fix snapshot browser blocked by ad blocker (snapshot names with colons/timestamps in URL)
- Browse now uses POST request instead of GET to avoid URL pattern matching
- PHP rewrite: remove all type annotations for PHP 7 compat, use ob_start for reliable error capture
- Snapshot name regex now allows colons (for existing snapshots like autosnap_2026-04-11_22:50:05)
- Switch to date-based versioning format YYYY.MM.DD.NN

## Version 2025.04.16
- Fix snapshot browser "Failed to fetch" (PHP 8 union type, realpath on .zfs virtual dir)
- Fix Run Now creating no snapshots (add --now flag to bypass time checks)

## Version 2025.04.15
- Fix "Missing CSRF token" on Run Now and Restore buttons
- Fix snapshot browser not opening (removed hidden state, added Browse button)
- Fix template datasets showing blank values (now shows global retention values)
- Fix dataset config loading (was fetching /boot/config directly over HTTP)

## Version 2025.04.14
- Add native ZFS snapshot management (no external tools required)
- Snapshot scheduler: frequent / hourly / daily / weekly / monthly / yearly retention
- Snapshot browser: browse any snapshot, restore files/folders to live dataset
- Fix converter cron accumulating duplicate entries on update

## Version 2025.04.13
- Fix containers being stopped unnecessarily when their bind mount points to the appdata root instead of a subdirectory

## Version 2025.04.12
- Add automatic schedule (cron) with hourly/6h/daily/weekly/custom options
- Cron job auto-restored on reboot via rc.d script
- Fix cron settings not persisting after page reload
- Fix plugin update via Unraid GUI (standard versioned txz naming)
- Fix HTML entity encoding in log viewer
- Fix misleading "Error" badge when nothing to convert

## Version 2025.04.11
- Initial release
- Convert regular folders to ZFS child datasets
- Docker container and VM awareness (auto stop/start)
- Resume interrupted conversions
- Dry-run mode
- Real-time log viewer
- Unraid notification support
</CHANGES>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
mkdir -p &configDir;
mkdir -p &tmpDir;
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&configDir;/&name;-&version;-x86_64-1.txz" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
<URL>&pkgURL;/&name;-&version;-x86_64-1.txz</URL>
<MD5>&md5;</MD5>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
rm -f $(ls &configDir;/&name;-*.txz 2>/dev/null | grep -v '&version;')
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/etc/rc.d/rc.&name;" Mode="755">
<INLINE>
#!/bin/bash
mkdir -p /tmp/zfs.dataset.converter
/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.dataset.converter/scripts/setup_cron.sh &gt;/tmp/zfs.dataset.converter/setup_cron.log 2&gt;&amp;1
/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.dataset.converter/scripts/setup_snapshots.sh &gt;/tmp/zfs.dataset.converter/setup_snapshots.log 2&gt;&amp;1
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
if [ ! -f &configDir;/settings.cfg ]; then
cat &gt; &configDir;/settings.cfg &lt;&lt; 'SETTINGS_EOF'
# ZFS Dataset Converter - default settings
dry_run=yes
cleanup=yes
replace_spaces=no
should_process_containers=yes
appdata_pool=cache
appdata_dataset=appdata
should_process_vms=no
vm_pool=cache
vm_dataset=domains
vm_forceshutdown_wait=90
buffer_zone=11
send_notifications=yes
validation_tolerance=5
extra_datasets=
cron_enabled=no
cron_preset=daily
cron_hour=2
cron_minute=0
cron_weekday=0
cron_custom=0 2 * * *
snapshots_enabled=no
snap_frequent=0
snap_hourly=24
snap_daily=30
snap_weekly=4
snap_monthly=3
snap_yearly=0
snap_daily_hour=2
snap_min_free_pct=5
snap_free_target=
snap_age_frequent=0
snap_age_hourly=0
snap_age_daily=0
snap_age_weekly=0
snap_age_monthly=0
snap_age_yearly=0
snap_schedule_preset=15min
snap_schedule_custom=*/15 * * * *
send_enabled=no
send_schedule_preset=daily
send_schedule_hour=4
send_schedule_custom=0 4 * * *
SETTINGS_EOF
fi

# Migration: older versions wrote cron entries straight into the root crontab.
# Those are now managed through /etc/cron.d, so drop the leftovers to avoid
# every job running twice.
( crontab -l 2>/dev/null \
  | grep -v '^# zfs-dataset-converter' \
  | grep -v 'run_auto\.sh' \
  | grep -v 'snapshot_manager\.sh' \
) | crontab - 2&gt;/dev/null

# Apply cron jobs from saved settings
/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.dataset.converter/scripts/setup_cron.sh &gt;/tmp/zfs.dataset.converter/setup_cron.log 2&gt;&amp;1
/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.dataset.converter/scripts/setup_snapshots.sh &gt;/tmp/zfs.dataset.converter/setup_snapshots.log 2&gt;&amp;1
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
# Remove cron entries (managed files first, then any legacy crontab lines)
rm -f /etc/cron.d/&name; /etc/cron.d/&name;-snapshots
( crontab -l 2>/dev/null \
  | grep -v "# zfs-dataset-converter" \
  | grep -v "run_auto\.sh" \
  | grep -v "snapshot_manager\.sh" \
) | crontab - 2>/dev/null
rm -f /etc/rc.d/rc.&name;
command -v update_cron &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1 &amp;&amp; update_cron &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1
[ -f /var/run/crond.pid ] &amp;&amp; kill -HUP "$(cat /var/run/crond.pid)" 2&gt;/dev/null
removepkg &name; 2&gt;/dev/null || rm -rf &pluginDir;
rm -rf &tmpDir;
echo "ZFS Dataset Converter removed. Settings in &configDir; preserved."
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
